          "id": "q1",
          "type": "radio",
          "label": "",
          "options": [
            { "value": "A", "text": "\\( 32x^2 \\)" },
            { "value": "B", "text": "\\( 16x^6 \\)" },
            { "value": "C", "text": "\\( 32x^6 \\)" },
            { "value": "D", "text": "\\( 8x^2 \\)" }
          ],
          "answer": "A"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Power rule first: (ab)^n = a^n · b^n. Then multiply by adding exponents.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "(4x³)² · 2x⁻⁴",
        "= 4² · x⁶ · 2x⁻⁴",
        "= 16 · 2 · x^(6 + (-4))",
        "= 32x²"
      ],
      "feedback_correct": "🔥 Exponent rules. Clean.",
      "feedback_wrong": "Apply power rule: (4x³)² = 16x⁶. Then multiply: 16x⁶ · 2x⁻⁴ = 32x²."
